   "last_comment_by": "qaisermehdi3-coder",
   "last_comment": "One fact for the open design question \"what counts as usage / how idle is defined\", for the inference case (your February vLLM case). vLLM exports its own work counters on /metrics: requests finished (request_success_total) and prompt and output tokens (request_prompt_tokens_sum, request_generation_tokens_sum). So for a vLLM pod there is a layer next to \"Used\": work served. \"0 requests finished in…",
   "summary": "D1 (billing basis), D1b (exceptions) and D2 (idle-reclaim consent) are still with MOC leadership, and the RfD recommends a tier model. New input: vLLM's own request and token counters tell idle from busy without DCGM, per server even on a shared GPU, but only for servers that export them.",
